direction: down
title: GPTpatient modernization · History Assessment

// Natural, bounded expansion of history only when the learner asks a relevant question.
h01: Learner asks symptom or history question { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
h02: Find matching seed cue and existing fact expansions { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
h03: Is a bounded history cue relevant to this question? { shape: diamond; style.fill: "#FFF0C2"; style.stroke: "#77520A"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
h04: Answer naturally in the fixed patient personality { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
h05: Propose only details compatible with the seed and question { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
h06: Send utterance and proposal through turn validation { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
h07: Append accepted fact to the correct history section { shape: cylinder; style.fill: "#DDEFEA"; style.stroke: "#175A50"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
h08: Reuse accepted detail on later turns; never rewrite seed { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
h09: No cue: answer from known facts without a profile dump { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
h10: Record each detail as fictional patient-reported history { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
h11: Keep sensitive questions patient-centered and case-relevant { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
h01 -> h02 -> h03
h03 -> h04: relevant cue
h04 -> h05 -> h06 -> h10 -> h07 -> h08
h03 -> h09: no expandable cue
h11 -> h01

// Coverage, assessment phase, post-session scoring, and debrief.
c01: Track pertinent symptoms · reproductive context · relevant history { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c02: Track exam / test findings · synthesis · differential · plan { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c03: Mark each topic asked · missing · sensitive · not relevant { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c04: Update encounter coverage state { shape: cylinder; style.fill: "#DDEFEA"; style.stroke: "#175A50"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c05: Learner uses visible button or says begin assessment { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c06: Is the phase-change cue explicit and unambiguous? { shape: diamond; style.fill: "#FFF0C2"; style.stroke: "#77520A"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c07: Ask learner to confirm an ambiguous spoken cue { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c08: Set phase to assessment after confirmation { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c09: Submit summary · differential / diagnosis · rationale · plan { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c10: Runtime-validate assessment request { shape: diamond; style.fill: "#FFF0C2"; style.stroke: "#77520A"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c11: Return field errors; keep assessment editable { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c12: Persist submission and assessment-complete event { shape: cylinder; style.fill: "#DDEFEA"; style.stroke: "#175A50"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c13: Enqueue scoring in separate post-session capacity lane { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c14: Score against educator-reviewed versioned case rubric { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c15: Return actionable debrief after submission { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c16: Preserve immutable seed and accepted expansions { shape: rectangle; style.fill: "#E8F0FC"; style.stroke: "#244C78"; style.font-color: "#14243A"; style.font-size: 68; style.stroke-width: 2 }
c01 -> c02 -> c03 -> c04
c05 -> c06
c06 -> c07: ambiguous
c07 -> c05: confirmation
c06 -> c08: explicit / confirmed
c08 -> c09 -> c10
c10 -> c11: invalid
c10 -> c12: valid
c12 -> c13 -> c14 -> c15 -> c16
